    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass with no failures. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature on the `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}` endpoint. An owner request may now include an optional `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the response exposes `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is supplied.\n\nChanges:\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a writable `title` property to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema. These drive the generated DTOs and the MapStruct mapping (which maps by name automatically).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, and a derived `getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to just `lastName` when the title is null/blank.\n- **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/postgres`, `db/mysql`) \u2014 added a nullable `title` column to the `owners` table so the persisted field round-trips (tests run against hsqldb; the rest updated for consistency).\n\nThe new `Cp45Tests` passes and the full suite is green (56/56).",
